+a)} \\geq \\frac{\\log b}{\\log (ca)}, \\quad \\frac{\\log c}{\\log (a+b)} \\geq \\frac{\\log c}{\\log (ab)}.\n\\]\n\nSo it suffices to show:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log a}{\\log (bc)} + \\frac{\\log b}{\\log (ca)} + \\frac{\\log c}{\\log (ab)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nIntroducing new variables $A = \\log a$, $B = \\log b$, and $C = \\log c$, the inequality turns into:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{A}{B + C} + \\frac{B}{C + A} + \\frac{C}{A + B} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nLet:\n\n\\[\nB + C = x, \\quad C + A = y, \\quad A + B = z,\n\\]\n\nAdding these equations:\n\n\\[\n2A + 2B + 2C = x + y + z.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we find:\n\n\\[\n2A = x + y - z, \\quad 2B = y + z - x, \\quad 2C = z + x - y.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{x + y - z}{2}, \\quad B = \\frac{y + z - x}{2}, \\quad C = \\frac{z + x - y}{2}.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute back into our inequality:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{y + z - x}{x} + \\frac{z + x - y}{y} + \\frac{x + y - z}{z} \\right) \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by 2, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{y + z - x}{x} + \\frac{z + x - y}{y} + \\frac{x + y - z}{z} \\geq 3.\n\\]\n\nRewrite and rearrange the terms yields:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{x} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x}{z} + \\frac{z}{x} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{z}{y} \\right) \\geq 6.\n\\]\n\nSince by AM-GM inequality:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{x} \\geq 2,\n\\]\n\nwe have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{x} + \\frac{x}{z} + \\frac{z}{x} + \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{z}{y} \\geq 6.\n\\]\n\nHence, the original inequality holds true. \n\nTherefore, we conclude:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\log_{b+c} a^{2} + \\log_{c+a} b^{2} + \\log_{a+b} c^{2} \\geq 3}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Let \\( \\xi_{n} \\downarrow \\xi \\) almost surely, \\( \\mathrm{E}\\left|\\xi_{n}\\right|<\\infty \\), for \\( n \\geqslant 1 \\), and \\( \\inf \\mathrm{E} \\xi_{n}>-\\infty \\). Show that \\( \\mathrm{E}\\left|\\xi_{n}-\\xi\\