\log_{5} 7 > \\log_{13} 17\\).\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{\\log_{5} 7 > \\log_{13} 17}\\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Rewrite the logarithmic expressions relative to base-5 and base-13**:\n   \\[\n   \\log_{5} 7 = 1 + \\log_{5} \\left(\\frac{7}{5}\\right)\n   \\]\n   and\n   \\[\n   \\log_{13} 17 = 1 + \\log_{13} \\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Compare the logarithmic components**:\n   We know that:\n   \\[\n   \\log_{5} \\left(\\frac{7}{5}\\right)\n   \\]\n   and\n   \\[\n   \\log_{13} \\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n   To compare these, we compare the arguments inside the logarithms:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7}{5} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{17}{13}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the numerical values of these fractions**:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7}{5} = 1.4 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{17}{13} \\approx 1.3077\n   \\]\n\n   Clearly,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7}{5} > \\frac{17}{13}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Use the monotonicity of the logarithm function**:\n   Since the logarithm function is monotonically increasing,\n   \\[\n   \\log_{5} \\left(\\frac{7}{5}\\right) > \\log_{13} \\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Combine these results to conclude the comparison**:\n   Thus,\n   \\[\n   1 + \\log_{5} \\left(\\frac{7}{5}\\right) > 1 + \\log_{13} \\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n   Hence, \n   \\[\n   \\log_{5} 7 > \\log_{13} 17\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\log_{5} 7 > \\log_{13} 17}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "The magnitudes $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ of the acute angles satisfy the equation\n\n\\[\n\\sin^2 \\alpha + \\sin^2 \\beta = \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)\n\\]\n\nProve that $\\alpha + \\beta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.", "deepseek_reasoning": "Alright, so I need to prove that \u03b1 + \u03b2 equals \u03c0/2 given that both \u03b1 and \u03b2 are acute angles and they satisfy the equation sin\u00b2\u03b1 + sin\u00b2\u03b2 = sin(\u03b1 + \u03b2). Let me start by u