sect.\n- \\(K\\) be the midpoint of \\(BC\\).\n- \\(O\\) represent the center of the circle inscribed in triangle \\(BCM\\).\n- \\(r\\) be the radius of the cone's base, and \\(2r\\) be its height.\n\n1. **Finding Distance \\(PD = PE = PK\\):**\n\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem,\n\n   \\[\n   PD = PE = PK = \\sqrt{r^2 + (2r)^2} = \\sqrt{r^2 + 4r^2} = r \\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identifying key lengths:**\n\n   Let \\(ME = MD = x\\).\n\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   BK = BE = 2x \\quad \\text{and} \\quad CK = CD = 2x\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, triangle \\(BMC\\) is isosceles.\n\n   \\[\n   MK = \\sqrt{(3x)^2 - (2x)^2} = \\sqrt{9x^2 - 4x^2} = x \\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculating the area of triangle \\(BCM, p\\) is half the perimeter, and \\(S\\) is the area:**\n\n   \\[\n   p = \\frac{1}{2}(BC + BM + CM) = \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 2x \\sqrt{5} + 2x \\sqrt{5}) = \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 4x \\sqrt{5})\n   \\]\n\n   Using area,\n\n   \\[\n   S = pr = 5xr\n   \\]\n\n4. **Comparing this with another form of the area \\(S\\):**\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{1}{2} BC \\cdot MK = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4x \\cdot x \\sqrt{5} = 2x^2 \\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n   Equating,\n\n   \\[\n   5xr = 2x^2 \\sqrt{5} \\implies x = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Evaluate \\(S_{\\triangle APB}\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle APB} = 2S_{\\triangle BMP} = 2 \\times \\frac{1}{2} MB \\cdot PE = MB \\times PE = 3x \\cdot r \\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{15r^2}{2}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Similarly Required Area \\( S_{\\triangle APC} = \\frac{15r^2}{2} \\)**:\n\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle BPC} = \\frac{1}{2} BC \\cdot PK = 2x \\cdot r \\sqrt{5} = r \\sqrt{5} \\cdot r \\sqrt{5} = 5r^2\n   \\]\n\n   Total lateral surface area,\n\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{15r^2}{2} + \\frac{15r^2}{2} + 5r^2 = \\frac{35r^2}{2}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Base Area Calculation \\( AB, AC, AK \\):**\n\n   \\[\n   AK = \\sqrt{AB^2 - BK^2} = \\sqrt{25r^2 - 5r^2} = 2r \\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n   Thus,\n\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle ABC} = \\frac{1}{2} BC \\cdot AK = r\\s